Feature: Altitude
  New waypoints go at the [[plan altitude]], which shows between ALT- and ALT+. These buttons
  change it in steps of 10 m, from 10 m to 300 m. All altitudes are relative to [[home]]. A
  change to the plan altitude does not move the waypoints that are already in the plan.

  Over hills, compare the plan with the terrain. The planner compares each waypoint with the
  ground below it, in the height map of the sim. It raises each waypoint that is too low.
  Mission Planner calls this Verify height.

  Expectation: ALT+ raises the plan altitude
    Given the plan altitude is below 300 m
    When the operator raises the plan altitude
    Then the plan altitude goes up by 10 m

  Expectation: ALT+ stops at 300 m
    Given the plan altitude is 300 m
    When the operator raises the plan altitude
    Then the plan altitude stays the same

  Expectation: ALT- lowers the plan altitude
    Given the plan altitude is above 10 m
    When the operator lowers the plan altitude
    Then the plan altitude goes down by 10 m

  Expectation: ALT- stops at 10 m
    Given the plan altitude is 10 m
    When the operator lowers the plan altitude
    Then the plan altitude stays the same

  Expectation: Waypoints already planned keep their altitude
    Given the plan has at least 1 item
    And the newest waypoint is at the plan altitude
    And the plan altitude is below 300 m
    When the operator raises the plan altitude
    Then the newest waypoint is at another altitude

  Expectation: A height check raises waypoints above the terrain
    Given the plan has at least 1 item
    When the operator checks the heights against the terrain
    Then the waypoints are clear of the terrain

  Expectation: A new waypoint needs a new height check
    Given the waypoints are clear of the terrain
    And the map tool is PLAN
    When the operator clicks the map
    Then the waypoints are unchecked
